Datasets are scored separately and combined afterwards, never merged before scoring. A 27K study and an EPIC study have different probe spaces, and feature coverage is a property of a dataset – merged, a clock that covers 99% of one study and 40% of another reports a single meaningless average, and the AA2 test compares cases in the well-covered study against controls in the badly-covered one.


